From: handheld-extra
Subject: [PATCH] steamcompmgr: run a capped game's panel only as fast as needed

Two changes to how _update_app_target_refresh_cycle() picks the panel rate on
a display with discrete rates (the AYN Odin 3: 60 and 120 Hz).

1. Steam's per-game Refresh Rate setting arrives with ONLY_CHANGE_REFRESH_RATE
   but went through the frame-limit rule, "the highest valid rate the target
   divides into", so picking 60 Hz left the panel at 120. A refresh-rate-only
   request now uses the exact rate when the panel has it.

2. For a frame limit, the new refresh_prefer_lowest ConVar (on by default)
   takes the lowest such rate instead of the highest: a 30 or 60 fps limit runs
   the panel at 60 Hz, 40 stays at 120. Each frame still shows for whole
   refreshes; the panel just does not refresh twice as often as it needs to.
   Set it to 0 for upstream's choice.

The second is what frame generation needs. lsfg-vk presents each real frame
and its generated one back to back and leaves the spacing to the display, so
its output only paces evenly when it equals the refresh rate: 30 fps x2 on a
120 Hz panel showed as 8.3 ms / 25 ms pairs (AYN Odin 3, 2026-10-23). With a
Steam limit of 60 the panel now runs at 60 Hz and the pairs are even.

---
--- a/src/steamcompmgr.cpp
+++ b/src/steamcompmgr.cpp
@@ -1264,6 +1264,8 @@
 bool g_nCombinedAppRefreshCycleChangeRefresh[gamescope::GAMESCOPE_SCREEN_TYPE_COUNT] = { true, true };
 bool g_nCombinedAppRefreshCycleChangeFPS[gamescope::GAMESCOPE_SCREEN_TYPE_COUNT] = { true, true };
 
+gamescope::ConVar<bool> cv_refresh_prefer_lowest( "refresh_prefer_lowest", true, "For a frame limit, run the panel at the lowest valid rate the limit divides into instead of the highest." );
+
 static void _update_app_target_refresh_cycle()
 {
 	if ( !GetBackend()->GetCurrentConnector() )
@@ -1290,15 +1292,27 @@
 	{
 		auto rates = GetBackend()->GetCurrentConnector()->GetValidDynamicRefreshRates();
 
-		// Find highest mode to do refresh doubling with.
-		for ( auto rate = rates.rbegin(); rate != rates.rend(); rate++ )
+		// A refresh-rate-only request is the user picking a rate, not a frame
+		// limit: use it as is when the panel has it, instead of doubling it.
+		if ( !g_nCombinedAppRefreshCycleChangeFPS[ type ] &&
+			 std::find( rates.begin(), rates.end(), uint32_t( target_fps ) ) != rates.end() )
+		{
+			g_nDynamicRefreshRate[ type ] = target_fps;
+			return;
+		}
+
+		// A rate the target divides into, so each frame shows for whole refreshes:
+		// the highest upstream, the lowest when refresh_prefer_lowest is on.
+		uint32_t uPicked = 0;
+		for ( uint32_t rate : rates )
 		{
-			if (*rate % target_fps == 0)
-			{
-				g_nDynamicRefreshRate[ type ] = *rate;
-				return;
-			}
+			if ( rate % uint32_t( target_fps ) != 0 )
+				continue;
+			if ( !uPicked || ( cv_refresh_prefer_lowest ? rate < uPicked : rate > uPicked ) )
+				uPicked = rate;
 		}
+		if ( uPicked )
+			g_nDynamicRefreshRate[ type ] = uPicked;
 	}
 }
 
